body:
Hello @ArthurZucker and @Cyrilvallez,

I hope you are both doing well.

I am adding an official update to this issue regarding the preparation of RWKV-7 for native integration into Transformers.

I personally coordinated with the RWKV organization team to prepare and publish a new set of official checkpoints following the repository format expected for native Transformers integration. In parallel, I have been coordinating and validating a candidate RWKV-7 implementation for Transformers.

We are currently restructuring our checkpoint conversion, validation, and publication process. Our older RWKV model repositories receive more than 8,000 downloads per month, and we would like to make training, evaluation, and inference substantially more convenient for our open-source community and for the companies and professional users working with RWKV.

The existing `rwkv` implementation in Transformers targets RWKV-4. RWKV-7 uses different token-mixing rules and recurrent-state update rules, so it requires a separate `rwkv7` model family.

The new official checkpoints are:

* [RWKV/RWKV7-13.3B-20260805](https://huggingface.co/RWKV/RWKV7-13.3B-20260805)
* [RWKV/RWKV7-7.2B-20260805](https://huggingface.co/RWKV/RWKV7-7.2B-20260805)
* [RWKV/RWKV7-2.9B-20260805](https://huggingface.co/RWKV/RWKV7-2.9B-20260805)
* [RWKV/RWKV7-1.5B-20260805](https://huggingface.co/RWKV/RWKV7-1.5B-20260805)

These repositories provide:

* weights in `safetensors` format;
* sharded weights with an index for the 2.9B, 7.2B, and 13.3B models, while the 1.5B model uses a single `model.safetensors` file;
* a standard Transformers `config.json`;
* a standard `tokenizer.json`;
* a `tokenizer_config.json` using `PreTrainedTokenizerFast`;
* `Rwkv7ForCausalLM` as the declared architecture.

They no longer contain or require:

* an `auto_map` configuration;
* a root-level `modeling_rwkv7.py`;
* remote Transformers modeling code;
* `trust_remote_code=True`.

The repositories do contain a standalone `inference/` directory, but it is not used by `AutoModel` and is not Transformers remote code. Once RWKV-7 is integrated into Transformers, these checkpoints will be ready for native loading without executing remote code. They are not yet natively supported by the current stable Transformers release.

My own candidate implementation has been validated with:

* 131 non-slow RWKV-7 tests;
* 2 independent NumPy reference tests;
* 5 slow integration tests on an RTX 5090 using the official 1.5B checkpoint;
* validation of the tokenizer and the `2048/32/64` configuration;
* logits validation;
* generation of 20 tokens;
* recurrent-cache validation.

I am not claiming that the complete Transformers test suite currently passes. The branch still needs to be rebased onto `main`, and three DeepSpeed tests were excluded because `mpi4py` was unavailable in the test environment.

I am also aware that PR #47780 is already open. I have not opened a competing PR from my account. I would therefore like to coordinate with you before submitting anything: should we continue with #47780, coordinate its closure or replacement, or should I open a new official PR from my fork?

For transparency, I used AI assistance during development. I personally coordinated the implementation scope with the RWKV team and reviewed and validated the resulting implementation and test results. I am asking for your approval on the preferred process before submitting a first PR.

Thank you very much for your time. Which approach would you prefer for coordinating the official RWKV-7 integration with #47780?
